{"skill":{"slug":"aws-infra","displayName":"AWS Infra"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769526133525,"changelog":"- Initial release of aws-infra skill.\n- Provides chat-based AWS infrastructure assistance using AWS CLI and console context.\n- Supports querying, auditing, and monitoring AWS resources (EC2, S3, IAM, Lambda, ECS/EKS, RDS, CloudWatch, billing, etc.).\n- All actions are read-only by default; any write or destructive changes require explicit user confirmation.\n- Includes clear safety rules and region/profile handling.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1975,"sha256":"5bb0f62aad9655f0296b4d461ecae29d2c66599bea0341e12cf2cf25a9ba4b02","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"assets/icon.svg","size":1020,"sha256":"10fc1a86319eccfef8a8c1df5ce2d81db9a7d32ccb48c1308d4b15774a38d417","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"references/aws-cli-queries.md","size":1718,"sha256":"02bfd365a601b7f3a220a76f58c04c3321ea450d93d8fd7cb7c3457c9ff61906","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1928,"sha256":"3535fe2277e898f2206e6909d25cb03249e486893c08b91b531f2cfee4735a1b","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789021980338,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"95d6824194ca3df4580f988556b06040c394d3b09ed9f6c0cd19ccc558bf608f","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/95d6824194ca3df4580f988556b06040c394d3b09ed9f6c0cd19ccc558bf608f","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: aws-infra\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle is designed for AWS CLI interaction, providing read-only queries and requiring explicit user confirmation for any write or destructive actions. The `SKILL.md` file contains strong safety rules explicitly instructing the agent to default to read-only, require confirmation for changes, prefer dry-runs, and never reveal or log secrets, actively mitigating prompt injection risks. The `references/aws-cli-queries.md` file lists standard AWS CLI commands, including write actions clearly marked as requiring confirmation. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, or obfuscation.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160131742},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":72,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":4,"checkedAt":1789021980338},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a disclosed AWS CLI helper that can access cloud account data, but its instructions are coherent, read-first, and require confirmation before changes.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Using local AWS CLI context and AWS profiles is sensitive and broad, but it is disclosed and proportionate for an AWS infrastructure assistance skill.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifact is Markdown instructions plus a static SVG icon; I found no bundled executable scripts, dependency installation, remote payload retrieval, or tool-wrapping behavior.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill defaults to read-only commands, tells the agent to require explicit confirmation for write or destructive actions, prefers dry-run where available, and instructs it not to reveal or log secrets.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The artifacts do not request persistence, background execution, system hooks, privilege escalation, or credential copying; write-capable AWS commands are presented as user-confirmed examples.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is AWS infrastructure querying, auditing, monitoring, and carefully confirmed changes; AWS CLI use, profile/region handling, read-only inventory, IAM, CloudWatch, billing, and service commands all fit that purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable letting the agent use your local AWS CLI identity to inspect AWS resources. Use least-privilege AWS profiles, prefer read-only roles for routine questions, and require careful review before approving any command that changes, deletes, scales, or modifies IAM, billing, or production resources.","findings":"[PE3] expected: The references to environment AWS settings and ~/.aws/config are for selecting the AWS CLI profile/region, not for extracting credentials; no instruction tells the agent to read, print, copy, or exfiltrate secrets.\n[AE1] unexpected: The referenced file references/aws-cli-queries.md is present locally and was inspected; it contains AWS CLI command examples rather than hidden or unavailable behavior.\n[TM1] expected: The S3 delete example is a real write/destructive AWS action, but it appears under 'Common write actions (confirm before running)' and is consistent with the skill's explicit confirmation rule.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789021980338}}}}}